(Every way of naming a map gives a copy: a declaration, Set, is, storing
 it in a value, returning it from a parameter; and a copy grows alone.)
To 'pass back' with a map called shelf.
    Return a map, shelf.

a map called stock is {"k": 1}.
a map called 'the copy' is stock.
Set 'the copy''s "k" to 2.
a number called kept is stock's "k".
Print "declared from a name: stock {kept}, 'the copy' {'the copy''s length}".

a map called spare is {}.
Set spare to stock.
Set spare's "j" to 2.
Print "set from a name: stock {stock's length}, spare {spare's length}".

a map called other is {}.
other is stock.
Set stock's "j" to 3.
Print "is from a name: stock {stock's length}, other {other's length}".

a value called held is stock.
Set stock's "m" to 4.
Print "stored in a value: stock {stock's length}, held {held}".

a map called returned is 'pass back' of stock.
Set returned's "n" to 5.
Print "returned: stock {stock's length}, returned {returned's length}".

a map called counts is {"seed": 0}.
a map called tally is counts.
For each number from 1 to 40, Set tally's "{number}" to number.
Print "grown: counts {counts's length}, tally {tally's length}".
